# Project Conventions

These rules are enforced automatically. Follow them in all code you write or modify.

## Include Style

- All project includes use angle brackets: `#include <path/to/File.h>`
- System/stdlib includes also use angle brackets: `#include <vector>`
- NEVER use quoted includes (`#include "..."`) for any header

## Header Guards

- Use `#ifndef` / `#define` / `#endif` include guards (NOT `#pragma once`)
- Guard name: full path from module include dir, uppercased, slashes/dots → underscores
  - e.g. `math/Vec3.h` → `MATH_VEC3_H`
  - e.g. `sensors/radar/RadarEcho.h` → `SENSORS_RADAR_RADAR_ECHO_H`
  - e.g. `scenarios/Detection.h` → `SCENARIOS_DETECTION_H`

## Code Style

- C++17
- Formatting: LLVM-based clang-format (4-space indent, 100 col limit, pointer left-aligned)
- Run `clang-format -i <files>` after editing to ensure compliance
- Namespace nesting: `namespace foo { namespace bar { ... } }` (no inline `foo::bar`)

## Control Flow Conventions

- **Single return**: Every function has exactly one `return` statement at the end.
  - Use a result variable, assign within conditionals, return at the end.
  - Example: `double result = 0.0; if (cond) { result = ...; } return result;`
- **No `continue`**: Invert the loop condition and nest the logic inside an `if`.
  - Instead of: `if (!cond) { continue; } <logic>`
  - Write: `if (cond) { <logic> }`
- **No `break`**: Restructure logic to avoid early loop exit.
- **No early returns in conditionals**: Do not `return` from inside an `if` block.
- **All `if`/`for`/`while` must have braces**: Even single-statement bodies.
  - Example: `if (cond) { do_something(); }` (NOT `if (cond) do_something();`)
- **Functions that check a condition and exit early should return `bool`**:
  - Return `true` if the condition is met and work is done, `false` otherwise.
- **Functions returning an object on success/failure should use `std::optional`**:
  - Return `std::optional<T>` instead of early-returning the object or sentinel values.

## Module Dependency Layering

Compile-time dependencies are strictly enforced by `scripts/check_deps.py`:

| Module | May depend on |
|--------|---------------|
| core | (nothing) |
| environment | core |
| sensors | core, environment |
| fusion | core, sensors |
| autonomy | core, fusion |
| platform | core, autonomy |
| sim | all modules |

- `sensors` headers go in `systems/include/sensors/<type>/`
- Each sensor type has its own directory: `radar/`, `camera/`, etc.
- Tests go in `<module>/test/<component>/` and link against their module library

## Sensor Architecture

- Every sensor measurement extends `core::measurement::Spherical` (range, azimuth, elevation)
- Every sensor device implements `sim::scenarios::ISensorDevice` with `sense() → vector<Detection>`
- `Detection` (in `sim/include/scenarios/Detection.h`) is the generic inter-sensor type
- Multiple sensors aggregate via `sim::scenarios::SensorSuite`
- `MeasurementAdapter` converts `Detection` → `autonomy::SLAM::SlamMeasurement`

## Autonomy Module Layout

- `systems/include/autonomy/SLAM/` — SLAM algorithm interfaces and stubs (SlamAlgorithm, SlamState, SlamMeasurement, EkfSlam, GraphSlam)
- `systems/include/autonomy/models/sensor/` — landmark models (LandmarkModel, LandmarkModelKnownCorr, LandmarkModelUnknownCorr)
- `Landmark.h` moved to `core/include/Landmark.h` (fundamental type used by both environment and autonomy)

## Build System

- Header-only libraries use `add_library(<name> INTERFACE)`
- Compiled libraries list `.cpp` files explicitly in `add_library()`
- Each module has its own `CMakeLists.txt` with optional `add_subdirectory(test)`
- Tests are standalone executables registered with CTest via glob discovery

## Testing

- Tests use `assert()` directly (no test framework yet)
- Each test `.cpp` is a standalone executable with an `main()` returning 0 on success
- Scenario tests live in `sim/test/scenarios/` and exercise the full pipeline
